],[-63,-136],[-63,-43],[-34,-7],[-9,-56],[-28,-29],[-31,-105],[-22,-25],[6,-107],[-22,-84],[-27,-39],[-9,-55],[-16,-34],[-1,-69],[-11,-39],[-34,7],[-25,-108],[-41,-73],[-45,-42],[-11,108],[-29,35],[-35,69],[-65,42],[-5,21],[-56,75],[-7,30],[-35,7],[-25,25],[-34,2],[-55,63],[-4,64],[-29,95],[-13,9],[-20,148],[1,61],[13,28],[-10,48],[17,52],[1,129],[14,34],[-8,57],[10,52],[-5,64],[14,58],[9,145],[-6,51],[11,35],[-20,168],[-28,85],[11,49],[-26,64],[-8,109],[6,80],[-53,29],[-1,81],[-15,25],[7,72],[-17,115],[-17,156],[-21,52],[-16,86],[-10,-10],[-27,39],[-18,-1],[-10,33],[9,77],[-40,94],[-1,57],[-21,46]]],"bbox":[-179.14735543087488,18.91084480135654,-66.95217009082936,71.38961213849689],"transform":{"scale":[0.0005609787315938856,0.00026239514866144504],"translate":[-179.14735543087488,18.91084480135654]},"_source":"Computed by scripts/derive-pieces.mjs from data/us/newberry.topojson (The Newberry Library, Atlas of Historical County Boundaries) and the days named in data/us/acquisitions.csv: each piece is land the U.S. polygons gained on one day, outside the 1783 domain, credited to its last entry, dated by the stretch of days on which the U.S. union is the same. Nothing drawn.","acquisitions":[{"key":"treaty1783","date":"1783-09-03","label":"won","name":"Treaty of Paris (1783)","instrument":"Treaty of Paris, 3 September 1783","from":"Great Britain","source":"Statehood Campaigns: Deck Outline (2026-11-18), Taxonomy 1; Office of the Historian","note":"The founding domain: every Newberry polygon alive on 3 September 1783 (the Newberry's first day). From the deck outline; not yet reviewed by the owner.","within":null},{"key":"louisiana","date":"1803-04-30","label":"bought","name":"Louisiana Purchase (1803)","instrument":"Treaty of 30 April 1803","from":"France","source":"Statehood Campaigns: Deck Outline (2026-11-18), Taxonomy 1; Office of the Historian, \"Louisiana Purchase\"","note":"$15 million. Newberry's la_purchase: \"boundaries were not clearly defined but unquestionably included the western half of the Mississippi drainage basin.\" From the deck outline; not yet reviewed by the owner.","within":null},{"key":"westflorida","date":"1804-10-01","label":"claimed","name":"West Florida (claimed 1803; held 1810 and 1813)","instrument":"Madison's proclamation (27 October 1810); Mobile occupied (1813)","from":"Spain held it","source":"Statehood Campaigns: Deck Outline (2026-11-18), Taxonomy 1; Office of the Historian, \"Acquisition of Florida\"","note":"The Newberry draws it as U.S. land from 1 October 1804 (Orleans Territory), following the U.S. claim that it came with Louisiana; Spain gave up its claim in 1819. From the deck outline; not yet reviewed by the owner.","within":null},{"key":"redriver","date":"1818-10-20","label":"split","name":"Red River basin (Convention of 1818)","instrument":"Convention of 1818","from":"Great Britain","source":"Statehood Campaigns: Deck Outline (2026-11-18), Taxonomy 1; Office of the Historian","note":"Newberry's mo_terr v2: \"Area exchanged with British North America\" at 49 degrees north from the Lake of the Woods to the Rocky Mountains. From the deck outline; not yet reviewed by the owner.","within":null},{"key":"florida","date":"1819-02-22","label":"bought","name":"Florida (Adams-Onís Treaty, 1819)","instrument":"Adams-Onís Treaty, signed 22 February 1819 (in force 1821)","from":"Spain","source":"Statehood Campaigns: Deck Outline (2026-11-18), Taxonomy 1; Office of the Historian, \"Acquisition of Florida\"","note":"The part of the day's gain inside the Newberry's Florida Unorganized Federal Territory (fl_uft): no money to Spain; the United States took on $5 million of claims. From the deck outline; not yet reviewed by the owner.","within":"fl_uft"},{"key":"adamsonis_line","date":"1819-02-22","label":"split","name":"Adams-Onís boundary line (1819)","instrument":"Adams-Onís Treaty, signed 22 February 1819 (in force 1821)","from":"Spain","source":"Statehood Campaigns: Deck Outline (2026-11-18), Taxonomy 1","note":"The part of the day's gain inside the Newberry's Missouri Territory (mo_terr v3: area exchanged with Spain along the treaty's line). From the deck outline; not yet reviewed by the owner.","within":"mo_terr"},{"key":"hempstead","date":"1819-06-01","label":null,"name":"Missouri Territory's claim south of the Red River (1819)","instrument":"Missouri Territory act of 15 December 1818, in force 1 June 1819 (Hempstead County)","from":"Spain, then Mexico, claimed it","source":"The Newberry Library (mo_terr v4)","note":"Not an acquisition and not in the outline's taxonomy: Newberry's mo_terr v4, \"HEMPSTEAD created by Missouri Territory from ARKANSAS and non-county area. Uncertainty of boundary between Mexico and the U.S. resulted in competing claims to area in Texas.\" Unlabeled, drawn as paper while the Newberry draws it as U.S. land; the land entered the Union for good with Texas (1845).","within":null},{"key":"texas","date":"1845-12-29","label":"joined","name":"Texas (1845)","instrument":"Joint resolution of 1 March 1845, accepted by the Texas convention 4 July 1845","from":"Republic of Texas","source":"Statehood Campaigns: Deck Outline (2026-11-18), Taxonomy 1; Texas State Library","note":"With the claims Texas sold in 1850 (9 Stat. 446): in New Mexico, Colorado, Kansas, Oklahoma and Wyoming that land is the Texas piece. From the deck outline; not yet reviewed by the owner.","within":null},{"key":"oregon","date":"1846-06-15","label":"split","name":"Oregon (1846)","instrument":"Oregon Treaty","from":"Great Britain","source":"Statehood Campaigns: Deck Outline (2026-11-18), Taxonomy 1; Office of the Historian, \"The Oregon Territory, 1846\"","note":"The 49th parallel to the Pacific. From the deck outline; not yet reviewed by the owner.","within":null},{"key":"mexican","date":"1848-07-04","label":"won","name":"Mexican Cession (1848)","instrument":"Treaty of Guadalupe Hidalgo","from":"Mexico","source":"Statehood Campaigns: Deck Outline (2026-11-18), Taxonomy 1","note":"The treaty ended a war (the $15 million paid does not make it a purchase under the taxonomy's rule). From the deck outline; not yet reviewed by the owner.","within":null},{"key":"gadsden","date":"1853-12-30","label":"bought","name":"Gadsden Purchase (1853)","instrument":"Treaty signed 30 December 1853","from":"Mexico","source":"Statehood Campaigns: Deck Outline (2026-11-18), Taxonomy 1; Office of the Historian, \"Gadsden Purchase\"","note":"$10 million for 29,670 square miles. From the deck outline; not yet reviewed by the owner.","within":null},{"key":"alaska","date":"1867-03-30","label":"bought","name":"Alaska (1867)","instrument":"Treaty with Russia","from":"Russia","source":"Statehood Campaigns: Deck Outline (2026-11-18), Taxonomy 1; Office of the Historian","note":"$7.2 million. From the deck outline; not yet reviewed by the owner.","within":null},{"key":"hawaii","date":"1898-07-07","label":"joined","name":"Hawaii (1898)","instrument":"Joint resolution signed 7 July 1898; transfer 12 August 1898","from":"Republic of Hawaii","source":"Statehood Campaigns: Deck Outline (2026-11-18), Taxonomy 1; Office of the Historian","note":"Joined means a government agreed; that government came out of the 1893 overthrow of Queen Liliʻuokalani (the outline's edge cases). From the deck outline; not yet reviewed by the owner.","within":null}],"shares":{"as_of":"the states in force on the Newberry's last day, held open to the present","states":[{"id":"al_state","name":"Alabama","km2":133863,"pieces":[{"key":"treaty1783","label":"won","km2":127952,"share":0.9558},{"key":"westflorida","label":"claimed","km2":5906,"share":0.0441}],"uncovered":0},{"id":"ak_state","name":"Alaska","km2":1479698,"pieces":[{"key":"alaska","label":"bought","km2":1479671,"share":1}],"uncovered":0},{"id":"az_state","name":"Arizona","km2":295368,"pieces":[{"key":"mexican","label":"won","km2":224035,"share":0.7585},{"key":"gadsden","label":"bought","km2":71333,"share":0.2415}],"uncovered":0},{"id":"